{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb4S6VR8UAkA38XL67nR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AX1z9D13nkSqN5Ymu97WV6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; cat > result.json <<'EOF'\n{\"candidate\": \"O on Cu(111)\", \"family\": \"adsorbate/metal surface\", \"tier\": \"trust\",\n \"property\": \"adsorption_energy\", \"value\": -4.44, \"units\": \"eV\", \"uncertainty\": 0.5,\n \"method\": {\"engine\": \"ASE 3.29 + mace-torch 0.3.15 (GPU, float64)\", \"model\": \"MACE-MP-0 medium (2023-12-03, PBE/PBE+U MPtrj-trained universal MLIP)\",\n   \"protocol\": \"Static 0 K relaxations (BFGS, fmax 0.01 eV/A). Bulk fcc Cu cell relaxed (a0=3.626 A). Cu(111) slab, 3x3 surface cell, 4 layers, bottom 2 fixed, 10 A vacuum each side, O at 1/9 ML. Sites fcc/hcp/bridge/top scanned; bridge relaxes into fcc. E_ads = E(O/slab) - E(slab) - E(O atom, isolated, model energy). Convergence checks: 2x2x4 (1/4 ML) and 3x3x5 slabs.\",\n   \"ensemble\": \"static 0 K (no ZPE, no thermal terms)\", \"timestep_fs\": null, \"n_atoms\": 37, \"sim_length_ps\": null},\n \"flags\": [\"isolated_O_atom_reference_outside_model_domain\"],\n \"note\": \"Most stable site is fcc hollow: -4.436 eV (3x3x4), with hcp at -4.422 (+0.014 eV) and top at -2.54. Bridge is not a minimum. Numerical convergence: 2x2x4 gives -4.428 and 3x3x5 gives -4.436, so size and coverage effects are under 0.01 eV. PREMISE CAVEAT: an MLIP's isolated-atom energy (here E(O) = -2.082 eV) is a fitted atomic reference energy, not a spin-polarized triplet O atom computed in DFT, so the atom-referenced number carries a reference error that size convergence cannot remove. VALIDATION: (1) Independent known result: the model's O2 binding energy, 2E(O) - E(O2), is 5.53 eV with d(O-O) = 1.237 A. Experiment gives De of about 5.2 eV (D0 = 5.12 eV). PBE, the model's training level, typically overbinds O2 by about 1 eV, so the model's atom reference agrees with neither e